Hey gang.

I was thinking the other day. I know everyone says that NH is so great b/c
of the complex object interaction. Well, I'm not so appreciative.

I know it's a lot, much more than typical FPS that the industry craps out
today. Not that the Devteam has does a bad job, or anything, it's just not
my cup of tea.

But my problem is that most items seemed to be governed by simple 'if/then'
rules. Like, 'if you are a werecreature, then if you eat wolfsbane, then you
are no longer a werecreature'. They're deterministic and boring after you
learn them. I would like to see some object interaction that's more creative
and open-ended. Something that allows you to create new, unheard of things.

I know this is the typical suggestion -- all idea and no implementation. So,
I'm hoping to start a discussion on this thread as to how this could be
done.

